{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And its innards.</b> Since this goes upon the king's table, it must be done with honor and cleanliness. But consecrated offerings that are burned outside — 'and its innards' and its dung is said of them, and likewise: 'ושרפו באש את עורותם ואת בשרם ואת פרשם.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The word וקרבו literally means 'and its innards'; the comment plays on the idea that this portion goes to the altar (or priest) and requires special care, unlike certain other offerings whose parts including innards are burned outside. The referent of 'this goes upon the king's table' and 'outside' is textual; I translate the note as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:47.444160219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}